{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"title":"Getting Started","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles synchronizes SQLite stores by recording local changes as events and exchanging them through a cloud backend. It works with both Core Data and SwiftData.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using SwiftData?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for a complete guide — you never need to touch Core Data directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide covers Core Data setup, starting with a complete working example using ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Develop-with-Claude-Code","text":"Develop with Claude Code"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/claude.com\/claude-code","isActive":true},{"text":", install the Ensembles skill first. It teaches Claude the API, the cloud backends, Ensembles 2 → 3 migration, the seed policy, and the common pitfalls, so it writes correct setup code and diagnoses sync issues without hand-holding:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/plugin marketplace add mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3","\/plugin install ensembles@ensembles"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Add Ensembles to Your Project","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-Ensembles-to-Your-Project"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the Ensembles package to your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or via Xcode’s package dependencies:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3.git"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Import the core module and one cloud backend:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit   \/\/ or EnsemblesLocalFile, EnsemblesMemory"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Complete Example: Core Data with CloudKit","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Complete-Example-Core-Data-with-CloudKit"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s a complete, working setup for a SwiftUI app that syncs via CloudKit. This uses "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which creates the Core Data stack for you and syncs automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"1. Create Your Core Data Model","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"1-Create-Your-Core-Data-Model"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Xcode, add a "},{"code":".xcdatamodeld","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" file to your project (e.g., "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Model.xcdatamodeld","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"). Define your entities as usual. For this example, we’ll assume a "},{"code":"Note","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity with "},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) and "},{"code":"uniqueID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"2. Define Your Model with `Syncable`","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Define-Your-Model-with-Syncable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For deduplication, conform your "},{"code":"NSManagedObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" subclass to the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and specify which property holds the global identifier. A UUID assigned at creation time is usually the best choice:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import CoreData","import Ensembles","","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","    @NSManaged var title: String","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A global identifier ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must never change"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" once it has been assigned. Changing it after sync has begun will cause duplicates or data loss.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a fixed, meaningful value instead of a UUID for singleton objects or reference data like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Set Up the Container","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"3-Set-Up-the-Container"},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let syncContainer: CoreDataEnsembleContainer","","    init() {","        \/\/ The model URL points to the .momd bundle compiled from your .xcdatamodeld","        let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","        \/\/ This creates a full Core Data stack automatically:","        \/\/ - SQLite store at Application Support\/MyNotes.sqlite","        \/\/ - Main-queue viewContext for your UI","        \/\/ - Auto-sync on save, on app activation, and on a 5-minute timer","        let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","            name: \"MyNotes\",","            modelURL: modelURL,","            cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","                privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","                schemaVersion: .v2","            )","        )!","","        self.syncContainer = container","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(","                    \\.managedObjectContext,","                    syncContainer.viewContext","                )","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That’s the complete setup. The container discovers ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances automatically, attaches to the cloud, and begins syncing. Remote changes are merged into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewContext"},{"text":" so your UI stays up to date.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Respond to Events (Optional)","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"4-Respond-to-Events-Optional"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Called after remote changes are merged into viewContext","container.didSaveMergeChanges = { notification in","    print(\"Merged remote changes\")","}","","\/\/ Called if a sync fails","container.didEncounterError = { error in","    print(\"Sync error: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Using-a-Custom-Store-Location","type":"heading","text":"Using a Custom Store Location"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need control over where the SQLite file lives, pass an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"storeURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(","    for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask",").first!","let storeURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent(\"MyApp\/data.sqlite\")","try FileManager.default.createDirectory(","    at: storeURL.deletingLastPathComponent(),","    withIntermediateDirectories: true",")","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Working-with-an-Existing-Core-Data-Stack","type":"heading","text":"Working with an Existing Core Data Stack"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you already have an "},{"code":"NSPersistentContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", pass it in directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    persistentContainer: myPersistentContainer,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Or if you have an existing ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSManagedObjectContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    viewContext: myContext,","    persistentStoreURL: myStoreURL,","    managedObjectModel: myContext.persistentStoreCoordinator!.managedObjectModel,","    managedObjectModels: nil,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Auto-Sync-Configuration","text":"Auto-Sync Configuration"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Control when syncing occurs with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    autoSyncPolicy: [.onSave, .onTimer],   \/\/ Sync on save and timer, not on activation","    timerInterval: 30                       \/\/ Timer fires every 30 seconds",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"code":"autoSyncPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".manual"},{"type":"text","text":" and call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" yourself for full control over timing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Backward-Compatibility-with-Ensembles-2","type":"heading","text":"Backward Compatibility with Ensembles 2"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re transitioning from Ensembles 2 and some users may still be on E2, set the compatibility mode:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This restricts exports to formats that Ensembles 2 peers can parse. Switch to ","type":"text"},{"code":".ensembles3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the default) once all users have upgraded.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Manual-Way-CoreDataEnsemble","text":"The Manual Way: CoreDataEnsemble"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control over the sync lifecycle, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","isActive":true},{"text":" directly. This is useful when you need to manage attach\/detach timing, handle specific delegate methods, or integrate with a complex Core Data stack.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Create-and-Attach","text":"Create and Attach"},{"code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","\/\/ Get the store URL from your persistent store coordinator","let store = persistentStoreCoordinator.persistentStores.first!","let storeURL = store.url!","let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MyNotes\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","\/\/ Attach registers this device in the cloud","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/ensembleIdentifier","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" must be the same on all devices that should sync together. If you have multiple persistent stores, create one ensemble per store with a unique identifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoid saving to the persistent store while attaching. If a save is detected, attachment will fail with an error and you will need to retry.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Sync-Changes","text":"Sync Changes"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" periodically — for example, when the app enters the foreground, on a timer, or in response to a push notification:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["try await ensemble?.sync()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A sync downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Sync errors are usually transient — just retry later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Handle-the-Delegate","text":"Handle the Delegate"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Implement ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to respond to sync events. The most important method merges remote changes into your main context:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension AppDelegate: CoreDataEnsembleDelegate {","    func coreDataEnsemble(","        _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","        didSaveMergeChangesWith notification: Notification","    ) {","        viewContext.perform {","            self.viewContext.mergeChanges(fromContextDidSave: notification)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Tip","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances are discovered automatically and no "},{"code":"globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implementation is needed. When you use "},{"code":"CoreDataEnsemble","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, the delegate method is required — but if your classes conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Syncable"},{"type":"text","text":" it is a one-liner:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func coreDataEnsemble(","    _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","    globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects objects: [NSManagedObject]",") -> [String] {","    ensemble.syncableGlobalIdentifiers(forManagedObjects: objects)","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"style":"tip"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other delegate methods let you:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inspect and repair merge data"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" before it’s committed (","type":"text"},{"code":"shouldSaveMergedChangesIn:reparationContext:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Handle save failures"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" during merging (","type":"text"},{"code":"didFailToSaveMergedChangesIn:error:reparationContext:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"React to forced detaches"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" caused by identity changes or data corruption (","type":"text"},{"code":"didDetachWithError:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for more on conflict handling and the reparation context.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Detach","text":"Detach"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To stop syncing, detach from the cloud:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["try await ensemble?.detachPersistentStore()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This removes local sync data (event logs and metadata). The persistent store itself is not affected. You can re-attach later to resume syncing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Seed-Policies","text":"Seed Policies"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" parameter controls how existing data in the store is handled during attachment:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (default) — Imports local data so it can be merged with data from other devices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Ignores local data. Use this when you want to start fresh from cloud data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Sync-Options","text":"Sync Options"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For advanced control, pass ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Download only — don't integrate or upload","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .cloudFileRetrievalOnly)","","\/\/ Force a rebase to compact sync history","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .forceRebase)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A rebase is the most expensive part of a sync, and Ensembles decides for itself when one is due. To choose the moment yourself, sync with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/suppressRebase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in normal use, and when conditions suit (the device is charging, a background processing task is running) read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/rebaseMetrics()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and pass ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/forceRebase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" if ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/RebaseMetrics\/isRebaseRecommended","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is true or your own thresholds are met.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Process-Pending-Changes","text":"Process Pending Changes"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS, the app may be suspended before Ensembles finishes recording a save. Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/processPendingChanges()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — for example, in a background task — to ensure all changes are fully stored:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["try await ensemble?.processPendingChanges()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Monitor-Activity","text":"Monitor Activity"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Track long-running operations via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/activityProgress","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or observe these notifications:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleDidBeginActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — An activity started","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleDidMakeProgressWithActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Progress updated (includes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AttachingPhase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — An activity finished (may include an error)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncLifecycle","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/gettingstarted"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/activityProgress":{"kind":"symbol","title":"activityProgress","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/activityprogress","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/activityProgress","abstract":[{"text":"The progress of the current activity, as a fraction between 0.0 and 1.0.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"activityProgress","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sf","text":"Float","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CoreDataEnsemble"}],"title":"CoreDataEnsemble","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CoreDataEnsemble"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The central class of Ensembles, representing a set of synchronizing persistent stores."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SeedPolicy/mergeAllData":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SeedPolicy.mergeAllData","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/seedpolicy\/mergealldata","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","abstract":[{"text":"Import the local store contents and merge them with cloud data at the next merge.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeAllData","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/sync(options:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sync","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"options","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SyncOptions","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Ensembles11SyncOptionsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/sync(options:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Syncs changes with other peers."}],"title":"sync(options:)"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SyncLifecycle":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncLifecycle","kind":"article","title":"Sync Lifecycle and Recovery","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/synclifecycle","abstract":[{"text":"Know when the app may save, how to detect sync success and failure, and how to recover a device that has fallen behind